{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837990",
      "title": "Validating Input Upon Form Submission",
      "sourceHash": "7bd58c32d1d537857aff3f2c7dab2785a93d3a48e8f3fbde9fc8648b1caa870f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.81,
          "end": 2.34,
          "en": "So here in this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "we added some validation to validate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 9.86,
          "en": "on keystroke combined with focus-based validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 12.33,
          "en": "So when we lose focus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.33,
          "end": 13.86,
          "en": "and we are providing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "a decent user experience here I'd argue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "Still, this is not the only way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 21.303,
          "en": "of adding validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "If we switch back from the StateLogin version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 30.21,
          "en": "of the login form to the ref-based login form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.21,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "we can also explore another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 35.16,
          "en": "of validating user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.16,
          "end": 38.28,
          "en": "For that, I'll tweak this import in the App component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.28,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "to import the login form from the Login.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "And in that file, I'm using refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "Now, since I'm using refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 51.27,
          "en": "I can't really validate on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.27,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "I would have to set up separate event listeners for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 56.37,
          "en": "And if we would do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.37,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "we could also just start managing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 60.693,
          "en": "the input values via state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "So if I wanna stick to refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "I can basically only validate the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "when the user submits the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.06,
          "en": "And indeed, that is a valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "and also quite popular strategy as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 78.963,
          "en": "You don't have to validate whenever the user types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 83.67,
          "en": "Instead here in the Login component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.67,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "in the handleSubmit function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "we could simply determine whether the email is invalid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "for example, by adding the emailIsInvalid constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "and then here when the form is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 101.61,
          "en": "performing our check, which here again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.61,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "is that we check if we don't have an @ symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 111.12,
          "en": "in that email with the includes method like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.12,
          "end": 113.40299999999999,
          "en": "and the exclamation mark in the beginning.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "Now we, of course, want to reflect this error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.22,
          "en": "in our form, and we can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.22,
          "end": 126.33,
          "en": "with some extra state because we need to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.33,
          "end": 130.23,
          "en": "if we find out that an invalid form has been submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.23,
          "end": 133.74,
          "en": "And we do that with state as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.74,
          "end": 136.593,
          "en": "So we must import the useState hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.46,
          "end": 141.48,
          "en": "And then with that, we can manage some state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.48,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "And that could be the formIsInvalid state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 149.13,
          "en": "if we wanna show some general error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "that affects the entire form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "Or of course, the emailIsInvalid state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 157.25,
          "en": "and setEmailIsInvalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.23,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "And initially, that's false, but we might wanna update this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 166.613,
          "en": "once we determined that the emailIsInvalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "Now here I have a name clash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 173.1,
          "en": "because I'm using emailIsInvalid twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.1,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "and therefore, to work around that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 178.32,
          "en": "I'll simply rename this here to emailIsValid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.32,
          "end": 180.03,
          "en": "and remove this exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.03,
          "end": 181.773,
          "en": "to perform the opposite check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 187.68,
          "en": "And then here I can check if not emailIsValid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.68,
          "end": 190.23,
          "en": "which of course means that it's invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.23,
          "end": 193.72,
          "en": "And in that case, I can call setEmailIsInvalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.94,
          "end": 198.063,
          "en": "and update this state by setting this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.31,
          "end": 205,
          "en": "We also might want to return here in this if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 207.99,
          "en": "because we might want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 211.74,
          "en": "that no other code thereafter gets executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.74,
          "end": 214.82999999999998,
          "en": "For example, if we would be sending an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.82999999999998,
          "end": 218.22,
          "en": "with the entered data, we might wanna prevent that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.22,
          "end": 221.673,
          "en": "from happening if invalid data has been entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.66,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "And by returning here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 226.983,
          "en": "we make sure that this code won't execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 231.21,
          "en": "So with that, I'm now validating the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.21,
          "end": 235.77,
          "en": "when the form is submitted and we can now use this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.77,
          "end": 238.5,
          "en": "which is only updated in that case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "if invalid data has been submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 245.073,
          "en": "We can use this state to again show an error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "And for that, I'll again add my div here with a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 254.33,
          "en": "of control-error and then check if emailIsInvalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.76,
          "end": 258.39300000000003,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I wanna output my error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 263.973,
          "en": "Please enter a valid email address like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.35,
          "end": 269.16,
          "en": "With that, if we go back, I don't get any error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 269.16,
          "end": 272.52,
          "en": "no matter what I'm doing with that email field here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 276.303,
          "en": "But if I click log in, I now get my error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.56,
          "end": 281.46,
          "en": "And this error message now also doesn't disappear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.46,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "until I submit the form again and I do so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 286.71,
          "en": "with a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 286.71,
          "end": 290.07,
          "en": "And even then here at the moment, it doesn't disappear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.07,
          "end": 292.95,
          "en": "though you can tell by this console log here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 292.95,
          "end": 295.14,
          "en": "that we made it past this if check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.14,
          "end": 297.633,
          "en": "and we did have a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 298.56,
          "end": 302.07,
          "en": "If I wanted to update the UI in that case, we could,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 302.07,
          "end": 307.07,
          "en": "of course, do that by simply setting emailIsInvalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 307.38,
          "end": 311.85,
          "en": "to false here after we make it past this check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.85,
          "end": 314.793,
          "en": "and we know that we have a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "By doing this, we make sure that if we submit a valid form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 322.14300000000003,
          "en": "the error message here goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 323.61,
          "end": 325.89,
          "en": "And that's how we can check the validity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 325.89,
          "end": 330.54,
          "en": "of the provided values when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.54,
          "end": 332.94,
          "en": "And in the end, it's up to you to decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.94,
          "end": 335.04,
          "en": "which approach you wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 335.04,
          "end": 339.543,
          "en": "and which user experience you wanna provide to your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 340.5,
          "end": 344.49,
          "en": "Validating on submission definitely takes a bit less code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 344.49,
          "end": 348.21,
          "en": "than validating on every keystroke and combining that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 348.21,
          "end": 351.54,
          "en": "with the focus state of the input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 351.54,
          "end": 353.49,
          "en": "But you, of course, are able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.49,
          "end": 356.94,
          "en": "to give the user a more direct feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 356.94,
          "end": 361.94,
          "en": "if you are using this keystroke focus-based approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 362.22,
          "end": 366.36,
          "en": "Nonetheless, validating upon submission is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 366.36,
          "end": 367.98,
          "en": "also totally fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 367.98,
          "end": 372.98,
          "en": "and can be the experience you wanna provide to your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 373.5,
          "end": 377.46,
          "en": "And it's also worth noting that you often might want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 377.46,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "to add submission-based validation even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 385.92,
          "en": "if you are already validating on keystroke and blur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 385.92,
          "end": 389.52,
          "en": "Because otherwise, if we switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 389.52,
          "end": 392.19,
          "en": "to this StateLogin form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 392.19,
          "end": 396.51,
          "en": "for a second where I am performing my validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 396.51,
          "end": 401.51,
          "en": "on keystroke and upon blurring the inputs, if you only rely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 402.9,
          "end": 406.71,
          "en": "on that validation, you got a nice user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 406.71,
          "end": 410.34000000000003,
          "en": "as the user is interacting with those inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 410.34000000000003,
          "end": 411.96,
          "en": "But you have a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 411.96,
          "end": 415.68,
          "en": "if the user simply clicks the submit button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 415.68,
          "end": 420,
          "en": "because in that case, as you see here in the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 420,
          "end": 425,
          "en": "the invalid data is handled here inside of handleSubmit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 426.06,
          "end": 429.27,
          "en": "So if the user simply ignores your hints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 429.27,
          "end": 433.47,
          "en": "and submits the invalid form, you might have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 433.47,
          "end": 436.08,
          "en": "That's why it's always a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 436.08,
          "end": 440.493,
          "en": "to also add validation here in this handleSubmit function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 441.42,
          "end": 444.15,
          "en": "I'm not going to do it here to save you some time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 444.15,
          "end": 448.74,
          "en": "because we did already do it here in the Login.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 448.74,
          "end": 452.1,
          "en": "And I'm also going to switch back to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 452.1,
          "end": 455.28,
          "en": "But it is definitely something you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 455.28,
          "end": 457.74,
          "en": "Adding submission-based validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 457.74,
          "end": 459.99,
          "en": "is always a good idea even",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 459.99,
          "end": 462.9,
          "en": "if you are already validating the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 462.9,
          "end": 464.79,
          "en": "on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 464.79,
          "end": 469.11,
          "en": "And in the next lecture, I'll show you an even easier way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
